  All rights reserved.

Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
modification, are permitted under the BSD-style terms reproduced in full at
the top of each of those files. The code is included only to provide the
POSIX regex API for MinGW / Windows builds, whose C runtime has none. Keep
the upstream headers and attribution intact when refreshing it.

## Other compatibility code

Not every tree under `lang/compat/` is vendored. `sha256/sha256.c` records
in its header that it was "Written fresh for lume-core (2026-10-15) ... no
upstream file was copied", public domain / CC0-style, no attribution
required; `ed25519/ed25519.c` is a from-scratch pure-C implementation of RFC
8032. Neither carries a third-party copyright notice; both are covered by
this repository's MIT license. Keep those headers intact when refreshing.
For the other `lang/compat/` directories, each source header remains
authoritative for its own status — this file makes no claim about them
either way.

The `agent-httpd` submodule is a separate repository with its own license
and notices, which are not duplicated here. System libraries such as OpenSSL
and SQLite are linked at build time and are not distributed in this
repository.
